//! # giochi-engine-capi
//!
//! The C ABI for GIOCHI-ENGINE, built as `cdylib` (`libgiochi.so`) and `staticlib`
//! (`libgiochi.a`).
//!
//! The surface is specified in `docs/C_ABI_CONTRACT.md` and explained in
//! `docs/C_ABI.md`; the header is `include/giochi.h`, generated by `cbindgen` from
//! this crate.
//!
//! ```c
//! #include "giochi.h"
//!
//! int main(void) {
//!     GiochiEngineConfig cfg = { .width = 960, .height = 540, .target_fps = 60,
//!                                .vsync = 1, .title = "my game" };
//!     if (giochi_engine_init(&cfg) != GIOCHI_ERROR_OK) {
//!         fprintf(stderr, "%s\n", giochi_get_last_error());
//!         return 1;
//!     }
//!     GiochiTexture t = giochi_texture_create("assets/player.png");
//!     /* ... */
//!     giochi_texture_destroy(t);
//!     giochi_engine_shutdown();
//!     return 0;
//! }
//! ```
//!
//! # Rules every function follows
//!
//! * Fallible functions return `int32_t`: `0` on success, a negative code from
//!   [`codes`] on failure, with the message in `giochi_get_last_error()`.
//! * Functions that return a handle return `0` on failure.
//! * Resources are opaque `u64` handles with explicit create/destroy; `0` is never
//!   a valid handle.
//! * Every call clears the thread's last error on entry, so a successful call always
//!   leaves `giochi_get_last_error()` empty.
//! * No Rust panic crosses the boundary: every exported function is wrapped in a
//!   `catch_unwind` guard that reports `GIOCHI_ERROR_INTERNAL`.
//! * The engine is single-threaded (ADR-010). Calls made before
//!   `giochi_engine_init` — or from another thread — report
//!   `GIOCHI_ERROR_NOT_INITIALIZED` rather than racing.
//!
//! # Which subsystem may be used where
//!
//! A scene callback runs inside the engine's frame, so it can only use what the
//! engine lends it:
//!
//! | Callback | Renderer | Input | Mixer | Texture registry |
//! |---|---|---|---|---|
//! | `on_enter` / `on_exit` | yes | — | yes | yes |
//! | `update` | — | yes | yes | yes |
//! | `render` | yes | — | — | yes |
//! | outside a run | yes | yes | yes | yes |
//!
//! The texture registry is shared rather than borrowed, so `giochi_texture_*` works
//! everywhere. Using a subsystem where it is not lent reports `GIOCHI_ERROR_SCENE`
//! with a message naming the callback it belongs in.
#![allow(unsafe_code)]
// The exported functions dereference caller-supplied pointers without being
// `unsafe fn`: that is what a C API is. Every one of them validates the pointer for
// NULL first and documents the contract in `docs/C_ABI_CONTRACT.md`; marking them
// `unsafe fn` would only make the C header wrong.
#![allow(clippy::not_unsafe_ptr_arg_deref)]
#![warn(missing_docs)]

